        <mxCell id="c_f61764f3e3" value="&lt;div style=&#39;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:23px;font-weight:700;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:8px&#39;&gt;THE SINGLE SENTENCE TO REMEMBER&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#39;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.28;color:#1F2937;text-align:left&#39;&gt;Executor Framework lets application code submit tasks while a controlled pool decides how many tasks run concurrently, where excess work waits, what happens under overload, how results are observed, and how execution ends.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFBEB;strokeColor=#D97706;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="180" y="565" width="1240" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_d928266a9d" value="&lt;div style=&#39;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#0F172A;margin-bottom:8px&#39;&gt;FINAL DECISION QUESTIONS&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&#39;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.28;color:#1F2937;text-align:left&#39;&gt;CPU or I/O? • How much concurrency? • What is the queue policy? • What happens when full? • What is the timeout/failure behavior? • Who owns shutdown?&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EAF2FF;strokeColor=#3B82F6;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
